foundation.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.1]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,3.0);
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (3.8,0);
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0) -- (1.6,1.6);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:1.6,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x+1.6},{1.6+0.35*\x*\x});
\node[font=\scriptsize,below right] at (0.5,0.7) {constant speed};
\node[font=\scriptsize,above left] at (2.6,2.1) {speeding up};
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-0.6,1.5) {Distance travelled};
\node[font=\small] at (1.9,-0.6) {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The straight part of the graph is a straight line, so it shows Owen travelling at a constant speed.
The curved part gets steeper as time passes, so it shows Owen speeding up as he jogs.

